{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>וַיִּשַּׁק לוֹ.</b> Meaning, he kissed him; but it is not proper to do so for any other dead person, for the deceased is laden with impurity, and his impurity pierces and rises up to the firmament, and the soul of the one who kisses would be harmed. Rather, him — Jacob — for he is alive; only that you call his state dormita, like one who sleeps and slumbers."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:51:13.477939833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}